A. Commit message:
rtla/timerlat: Fix histogram ALL for zero samples in older version

B. Change summary:
This patch backports the fix from the newer version to ensure that the minimum, maximum, and average latency values are not calculated when there are zero samples. It introduces a new function `format_summary_value` to handle formatting of these values, ensuring that dashes are displayed instead of nonsensical or undefined values.

C. Compatibility Risk:
Low

D. Fixed Code:
```diff
diff --git a/tools/tracing/rtla/src/timerlat_hist.c b/tools/tracing/rtla/src/timerlat_hist.c
index 8b66387e5f35c..4403cc4eba302 100644
--- a/tools/tracing/rtla/src/timerlat_hist.c
+++ b/tools/tracing/rtla/src/timerlat_hist.c
@@ -281,6 +281,21 @@ static void timerlat_hist_header(struct osnoise_tool *tool)
 	trace_seq_reset(s);
 }
 
+/*
+ * format_summary_value - format a line of summary value (min, max or avg)
+ * of hist data
+ */
+static void format_summary_value(struct trace_seq *seq,
+				 int count,
+				 unsigned long long val,
+				 bool avg)
+{
+	if (count)
+		trace_seq_printf(seq, "%9llu ", avg ? val / count : val);
+	else
+		trace_seq_printf(seq, "%9c ", '-');
+}
+
 /*
  * timerlat_print_summary - print the summary of the hist data to the output
  */
@@ -328,29 +343,23 @@ timerlat_print_summary(struct timerlat_hist_params *params,
